{"adr":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence","blob_sha256":"47c8903501b5d2fa3c5c72c9c59a5a0eebddae0c8ffa6f4f153f262068b1c16f","body_sha256":"ffea49cb49c014fdadba456a42c77eda38ad5c5ef11af22a599fca427bd42e69","event":"acceptance","obligations":[{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o01","section":"Decision","text":"The stored ADR governance states remain `proposed`, `accepted`, `superseded`, and `rejected`.","text_sha256":"001f7ed52690192b77d47b335e4330ab013d21b545941f42de41184ef734ee5c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o02","section":"Decision","text":"`accepted` is displayed as **Accepted/Planned**: it never implies implementation or verification.","text_sha256":"d610902fd6d5cff09b943043406d1d2b90db998ea93d76ec180c1db0dcd71830"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o03","section":"Decision","text":"Implemented and Verified are derived delivery states, not mutable ADR frontmatter values.","text_sha256":"de7d863ebea816f64cd245d1ca13074476ba5b9ccaaa0d11b15873a0f5e3c105"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o04","section":"Decision","text":"A separate append-only `.codearbiter/decisions/adr-lifecycle.jsonl` is the machine-readable delivery\nledger.","text_sha256":"759cc6fce7eadfbead672933213d2cd616b590254c0c48cc4f0932008aa6e77e"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o05","section":"Decision","text":"Future acceptance appends exactly one immutable acceptance binding for the ADR's canonical\nfull filename stem.","text_sha256":"45c3c7775b4159397b427ae7e332fbd1f309d98a5a22c44f6ebd7a6e4a7aa197"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o06","section":"Decision","text":"That binding records the acceptance commit, the SHA-256 of the exact committed\nGit blob, a separately specified SHA-256 over the immutable decision body, and the digest of a sealed\nauthoritative obligation set.","text_sha256":"46f0d0585671f37c1506509efcda71e744ea4fae40c15bf5886624781c4f5d09"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o07","section":"Decision","text":"A second acceptance binding for the same stem is invalid.","text_sha256":"5f36f155a35f549140829f5d97b66b6c0e703821164ad82cdfaf961d61dae841"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o08","section":"Decision","text":"Each normative obligation has a stable stem-scoped identifier and an exact ADR section/content\nbinding.","text_sha256":"62ff0c9ea9c42e9266c95e9f555db7c92afeff85cfd20fbd62f10c167389038c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o09","section":"Decision","text":"An ADR is Implemented only when every obligation in its sealed set has append-only,\ninput-bound implementation evidence.","text_sha256":"bdd29b07499b0ea78925abccd16aa7bc68babe9ed7dd25ff7f04d6ee1b62824b"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o10","section":"Decision","text":"It is Verified only when every sealed obligation has fresh,\ninput-bound verification evidence produced under an explicit proof contract.","text_sha256":"37e2f1d54e0cd2cab9b5f2fa05f58d2b7ffdc68ef4c30648f1a8804aef9d086e"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o11","section":"Decision","text":"Evidence records bind\nthe source commit, relevant input digests, producer, command or workflow identity, observation time,\nand freshness rule.","text_sha256":"f18a8ac1b5473f4a9baa7ff903ed6d4f77b23b71c6e9bf8220ac154c715937ea"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o12","section":"Decision","text":"Changed inputs invalidate the derived state; they do not rewrite history.","text_sha256":"f15da72d695b8ce858a7e3d79c0c8999fa19c537f533ea28d343ead5e15644ff"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o13","section":"Decision","text":"Public and machine-readable reports expose only obligations that are currently Verified at the input\ndigests being reported.","text_sha256":"4c6e69dd44f9e3cb4d9720e812543a9df8cb4fa930d62d21e865ef0cfd9ae641"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o14","section":"Decision","text":"Unsealed, stale, incomplete, or mismatched obligations fail closed with a\ndiagnostic.","text_sha256":"67235db51f60f946f2f294c6344f1c1da267e4cf7d6cb0bb77d3e228600c3387"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o15","section":"Decision","text":"A repository proof establishes only the narrow repository claim it actually measures; it\ndoes not imply live-host, publication, support, legal, or other external truth without that boundary's\nown approved proof contract.","text_sha256":"f24963b52c4c343b279b06b4dfa803bd81ad65fef66b8a72ba259bdca433b21c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o16","section":"Decision","text":"Legacy accepted ADRs receive explicit migration `baseline` bindings, never fabricated\nacceptance-time records.","text_sha256":"d92ab8f89a8e7ba7907307e940debc7173793aed00c0f939bab177b9a0595f89"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o17","section":"Decision","text":"Their obligation sets are mapped incrementally and remain unsealed and\nAccepted/Planned until independently reviewed.","text_sha256":"ab10cc734ec0b9fd9bd43dcf067d23ae3b1e4ba1e0d9c00f85cfd9ce659434b5"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o18","section":"Decision","text":"Age, an old pull request, or a matching digest alone\nnever promotes a legacy ADR to Implemented or Verified.","text_sha256":"bb3e961f251a8f72ef5c985335a9e657765a2d080943497c364f4f32bfc50529"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o19","section":"Decision","text":"The canonical ADR identifier remains the full filename stem.","text_sha256":"63914630a3157e123cdbc5beebde43667b1cec00ea5942c7d8d36ed816d29eba"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o20","section":"Decision","text":"Bare-number compatibility remains only\nwhile a number resolves uniquely.","text_sha256":"827fc3460d342bf5ffebe87bbedab937bfc801903d1e491bfa309348af99f64a"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o21","section":"Decision","text":"The two historical `0014` files retain their distinct full-stem\nidentities; neither is renamed or deleted and ambiguous bare-number resolution is never restored.","text_sha256":"b671e2886fc2fd51f3364b6ffad1e90836d9a8e83c6ceeda081b1fa1690bf7ef"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o22","section":"Decision","text":"ADR-0026's already-approved implementation uses ADR-0030's current four-item destructive set:\nlogged bypass (`/override`), merge to the default branch, branch or worktree deletion, and release and\ntag publication.","text_sha256":"e55f9c7d05f712b469749e3b3bd97a89d7ace65ec4718eaa17bb1cbc84be3d1a"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o23","section":"Decision","text":"The routing-table registry is authoritative, the arbiter keeps the required resident\nprojection, and CI proves item-for-item parity with a seeded mismatch.","text_sha256":"11c5b925f77cd00d3c8f14f3d8303dc653aabb771f6e73fae6813182eeba155e"}],"obligations_sealed":true,"obligations_sha256":"8a7eb7ec3f9e5cf9c146f89087d62e766e283eac33ad8d642f223089b072a17c","recorded_at":"2026-09-02T11:30:00Z","schema":"adr-lifecycle/v1","source_commit":"1eb4d6c6362be895b8d0caafabbf5d8b55bb9948"}
